# =============================================================================
# network_pipeline.R
# Crop-country transferability network paper -- full analysis pipeline
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Step 1  Negative-transfer (NT) computation, 8 crops x R=5 pool draws   [HEAVY, ~19 h]
# Step 2  Community detection + null model 1 + ARI/NMI vs climate/GDP clusters
# Step 3  Mechanism analysis (source/target signatures, partial correlation)
# Step 4  Eta-squared: GDP vs climate, with 5-seed stability check
# Step 5  Pool-size sensitivity pilot (pool 10/15/20; wheat, rye, sorghum) [HEAVY, ~4 h]
# Step 6  Community-assignment stability across R (ARI/NMI, R=1 and R=3 vs R=5)
# Step 7  Null model 2 (degree-preserving topology randomization)
# Step 8  Diagnostics: pair-count audit, prevalence by R, XGB/LASSO dispersion, yield skew
# Step 9  Figures 1 and 2 (publication versions: PDF, EPS, 1600-dpi TIFF, 300-dpi PNG; base R graphics only)
# Step 10 OPTIONAL data check: where the GDP values come from (constant-US$ series, PPP fallback, interpolation)  [needs internet + WDI package; off by default]
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE: run the whole file. Heavy steps 1 and 5 are skipped automatically if
# their output already exists; set RUN["step5"] <- FALSE below to skip Step 5 for now.
# Steps run in the order set by RUN_ORDER (the heavy Step 5 is placed last).
# =============================================================================

